# DBUG1 (stream S2-bodies, worker W13, EQ fuzz row ref-passes-fewer 0x0081de70) - the arguments of a call that the decomp
# gave to the virtual call made just before it (docs/PATCHES.md "DBUG1"). A virtual donor is outside POP2's reach
# (s2_bodies.py leaves a family with a virtual declaration alone: an overload would add a vtable slot), so this one is a
# site patch.

@@ DBUG1 src/staging/blk_00800000_od.cpp file
# x86 0x0081de70 (the destructor): after the Check() test it pushes 1 and 0, calls the virtual at slot +0x14 of the
# object at m_a0 + 0x18 with ecx = that object and no further push (a plain `call eax`, so the slot takes no stack
# word), pushes the result and calls 0x00445300 on the global at 0x011c3b3c. 0x00445300 is `ret 0xc`: it reads
# [ebp+8] (the pointer-sized first word), the byte at [ebp+0xc] and the word at [ebp+0x10]. So the two pushes are its
# second and third arguments, (eax, 0, 1); the decomp passed them to the virtual (v5(0, 1)) and declared Log with the
# one word. The virtual gets no parameters and Log three (int, bool, unsigned int; its decorated name changes,
# units_renames.tsv).
<<<
    void Log(int v);
===
    void Log(int v, bool b, unsigned int c);
>>>
<<<
    virtual int v5(int a, int b);
===
    virtual int v5();
>>>
<<<
            g_logger->Log(((SecondaryBase*)(m_a0 + 0x18))->v5(0, 1));
===
            g_logger->Log(((SecondaryBase*)(m_a0 + 0x18))->v5(), false, 1);
>>>
